<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Oettingen-Wallerstein</h1><p class="st-meta">1522 CE – 1806 CE (approx.) · capital Wallerstein</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Catholic line of the Ries counts of Oettingen, raised to princes in 1774, whose court at Wallerstein kept a renowned orchestra.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The 1522 division of the house of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-oettingen">Oettingen</a> gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wallerstein">Wallerstein</a> line lands in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nordlinger-ries">Ries</a>, with castles at Wallerstein and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harburg-swabia">Harburg</a>. While the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-oettingen-spielberg">Oettingen-Oettingen</a> line became Lutheran, Wallerstein remained Catholic and supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counter-reformation">Counter-Reformation</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The counts, raised to princes in 1774, ruled a farming territory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-circle">Swabian Circle</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wallerstein">Wallerstein</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harburg-swabia">Harburg</a> castle. Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kraft-ernst-prince-of-oettingen-wallerstein">Kraft Ernst</a> maintained one of the finest court orchestras in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, employing the composer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-rosetti">Antonio Rosetti</a>, and the family built up a famous library rich in medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Mediatised in 1806, Oettingen-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wallerstein">Wallerstein</a> came under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bavaria">Kingdom of Bavaria</a>. Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-of-oettingen-wallerstein">Ludwig of Oettingen-Wallerstein</a> served as a Bavarian minister in the 1830s and 1840s, and the family still owns <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harburg-swabia">Harburg</a> castle.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1522 CE – 1806 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.99%;width:5.65%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1522 CE – 1806 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Wallerstein</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kraft Ernst, Ludwig of Oettingen-Wallerstein</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Swabian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Oettingen-Wallerstein</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1664&amp;focus=principality-of-oettingen-wallerstein" aria-label="Principality of Oettingen-Wallerstein on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4922 471 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Oettingen-Wallerstein lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5242 727L5245 725M5242 727L5229 694M5242 727L5269 749"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5245 725h0M5229 694h0M5269 749h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5242 727h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5242 727h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Wallerstein. <a href="/atlas?year=1664&amp;focus=principality-of-oettingen-wallerste